# market/sealed — one sealed bid per cell (K-PRED-HASHEQ; PRIVACY §3.4).
# Fields: 2 commit, 3 value, 4 blinder (field 1 is written at birth). {FOUNDER} = the market founder's subject;
# {LAST_SEALED_HEIGHT} = D - 1, the last block height at which a bid may be sealed.
#   phase 1 (request/height <= D-1): commit is write-once; value and blinder stay 0.
#   phase 2 (request/height >= D):   commit never changes; value and blinder must open it:
#     commit = cSHAKE256(S = "DREGG.PRED.HASHEQ/v1";
#                        cell:8 ‖ len:4 ‖ "resource/field/3/after" ‖ len:4 ‖ "resource/field/4/after"
#                        ‖ len:4 ‖ "resource/field/2/after" ‖ (value + 2^255):32 ‖ blinder:32)
#     big-endian, read as an integer; blinder = 32 uniform bytes, never reused.
# The installable form is law.json beside this file. The shell grammar (P-LAW, law.rs) has no
# `hashEq` clause yet; this line is the spelling it should take.
any [ verb == read,
      all [ verb in {delegate,install,revoke}, subject == {FOUNDER} ],
      all [ verb == write,
            any [ all [ slot "request/height" <= {LAST_SEALED_HEIGHT}, field 2 writeOnce,
                        field 3 == 0, field 4 == 0 ],
                  all [ not (slot "request/height" <= {LAST_SEALED_HEIGHT}), field 2 delta == 0,
                        hashEq field 3, field 4, field 2 ] ] ] ]
